<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="162" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>AI analysis routes: implement the AnalysisAccess check (GitHub #233 item 1) and make each of the six /api/ai/analysis routes authorize, as the caller, the exact records it reads or writes (GET, export, save, fork, promote, execute), failing closed, with writes checked by the G5 pattern</title>
    <phase>Route authorization sweep (owner round 9, 2026-10-03); authored 2026-10-02, adversarially reviewed 2026-10-02</phase>
    <gate>startable (no task dependency; see the rebase rules in parallel-reason and the dependencies block)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs change on live BFF routes (tags bff-api, auth, security), plus a Spaarke.Core/Auth policy key. Closes 2 critical, 1 high and 3 medium sweep findings: any signed-in caller reads, exports or writes any analysis, and creates analyses against records it cannot see.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive and per-route: six routes with four different target shapes (a route analysis id resolved to its parent records, a body document id, a body session id plus a body or session-derived anchor, and a body playbook id with a branch-dependent write). Each route must authorize exactly the records its handler consumes, with the right Dataverse right.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs (a project parallel-safe:false zone, completeness-tested); Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs, which task 146 also edits (owner stamping at :1207 and :1405); Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs, which task 164 (playbook execute / agent run-playbook) is expected to extend; tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs, which task 167 and every sweep surface task edit; and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SessionOwnershipGuardTests.cs. It READS but does not edit Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs. Whichever of 146, 164, 167 and 162 lands second rebases onto the first.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, ai, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Route authorization sweep 2026-10-02 (notes/route-authorization-sweep-2026-10-02.md, workflow run wf_c2daa097-2f4), confirmed findings #1 (critical, export), #2 (critical, GET), #22 (high, promote), #50 (medium, save), #51 (medium, fork), #52 (medium, execute). Owner round 9 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md): UAC-r2 fixes all 82, now, with the stated fix pattern (reads: the caller's own Dataverse rights decide; writes: a rights pre-check as the user, then the app-only write, the 130/146 G5 pattern). Round 3b G5 and round 7 item 3 define G5 for app-created rows: Create privilege on the new row's table plus AppendTo on each parent its lookups point at, checked as the user. Also closes GitHub #233 item 1 (the AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs:203 "document lookup pending" TODO), which until now was tracked only as a generic TODO.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Today any signed-in user can read, export (as a file or by email) and save into SPE any sprk_analysis by its id, because the filter on those routes only parses the id and calls next. Fork and promote create analyses, app-only, against any document, matter or project the caller names, and promote can rebind another user's chat session. Execute overwrites a document's AI profile fields with only Read on it, and runs any playbook. Make every one of these six routes ask Dataverse, as the caller, about the exact record or records it acts on, before any read or write, and fail closed. Unknown and denied ids get the same answer. Writes use the G5 pattern: check as the user, then write as the app.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Do NOT rename or move FinanceAuthorizationFilter, and do not create a RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter or any other generalized copy of it: reuse it as it is. The rename is follow-up task 170, after the sweep tasks are integrated. Several sweep tasks reuse this filter in parallel, and a move in one of them would conflict with all the others.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 167 (the every-route guard) runs IN PARALLEL with this task. If RouteAuthorizationGuardTests on your branch has no Pending waiver for your routes (167 not yet landed), do NOT add waivers, ledger entries or Permanent waivers, and do NOT add your files to GovernedFiles. Instead, add a table "Route authorization ledger input" to your task note, with one row per route you changed or deleted: the route key exactly as the guard spells it (VERB /path), the mechanism that now decides (filter, probe or impersonation), the deny test (its fully qualified name, proving a caller without rights is refused), and, for a list whose query runs AS the caller, the words "handler decision: query runs as the caller". The main session records these in 167's ledger at integration. If 167 HAS landed on your branch, follow its ledger contract: delete your Pending waivers and set ResolvedBy and ProofTest in the same diff.</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 (BINDING): delete a route when it has NO caller in the repo AND it is NOT in any published API description; fix it otherwise. Search the repo for OpenAPI documents and Copilot or agent plugin manifests (for example *openapi*, ai-plugin*, *manifest*.json, declarativeAgent*) before you decide. List every deletion, with its no-caller and not-published evidence, in the note and the PR. Delete the services, filters and options that only the deleted routes used. Keep the file census count in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests right if a whole endpoint file goes.</amendment>
    <amendment>Impersonation: never assign ServiceClient.CallerId or CallerAADObjectId outside Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs (task 160 adds the single SDK entry point there, plus an arch rule). For the Web API, impersonate through DataverseWebApiService's existing impersonateSystemUserId parameter (MSCRMCallerID). It refuses Guid.Empty (task 104).</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: BFF endpoint filters (ADR-008), the task-130 per-route authorization evaluator (FinanceAuthorizationFilter: Document, Record and Privilege paths), the AI authorization seam (IAiAuthorizationService) and the Spaarke.Core caller-scoped access seam (AuthorizationService, OperationAccessPolicy). Expert in Dataverse RetrievePrincipalAccess over OBO and ProblemDetails (ADR-019). Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task, for each route below, a caller without the required rights on the route's targets gets the fail-closed answer before any Dataverse read of content, any Dataverse write, any SPE write, any AI call or any outbound message, and a caller with the required rights gets the same response as today:
(1) GET /api/ai/analysis/{analysisId:guid}, POST /{analysisId:guid}/export and POST /{analysisId:guid}/save: the filter resolves the analysis to its parent records (its "anchors") and requires Read on EVERY populated anchor. Any failure is the same uniform 404 as an unknown id. Save additionally requires AppendTo ("entity.associate_document") on the matter whose SPE container receives the file, only if that link exists live (see constraints).
(2) POST /api/ai/analysis/fork (G5): the caller holds the Create privilege on sprk_analysis, and Read plus AppendTo (new key "analysis.attach") on the body DocumentId; a body PlaybookId must pass the playbook-use decision. The #863 prior-session ownership check stays.
(3) POST /api/ai/analysis/promote (G5): the session must belong to the caller (otherwise the 404 a missing session gets); the Create privilege on sprk_analysis; "analysis.attach" on the body or session-derived DocumentId and on the body regarding matter or project; a body PlaybookId must pass the playbook-use decision.
(4) POST /api/ai/analysis/execute: Read on every body document (unchanged); Write on the document for the document-profile branch; and on the playbook-engine branch the caller must pass the playbook-use decision, and needs Write on every document when the playbook has a side-effecting node, an unresolvable node, or no nodes at all (legacy mode writes the document's profile fields).
(5) POST /api/ai/analysis/create is unchanged.
(6) The six routes pass RouteAuthorizationGuardTests (and lose any Pending waiver task 167 added for them), SessionOwnershipGuardTests names /promote, and a real-host completeness test fails if a future route in this group has no deny case.
(7) The behaviour is proven live in dev with non-admin test users (manual gate, main session).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Every anchor below was read on the working tree 2026-10-02 (branch work/unified-access-control-r2 @ b18a7d321). Line numbers drift; re-verify in step 0.

THE ROUTES. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs`: group `/api/ai/analysis` with only `.RequireAuthorization()` (:35-37; the BFF has no DefaultPolicy/FallbackPolicy, so this means "signed in"). Routes: /create :40-41 (`AddAnalysisExecuteAuthorizationFilter`, NOT a finding, must stay unchanged), /fork :59-60 (`AddAiAuthorizationFilter`), /promote :78-79 (`AddAiAuthorizationFilter`), /execute :93-94 (`AddAnalysisExecuteAuthorizationFilter`), /{analysisId:guid}/save :108-109, /{analysisId:guid}/export :123-124 and GET /{analysisId:guid} :138-139 (all three `AddAnalysisRecordAuthorizationFilter`). These seven are the only routes under /api/ai/analysis (no other file maps that prefix). Mapped whenever `DocumentIntelligence:Enabled` and `Analysis:Enabled` (default true) (`Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:243-246`); that is the production configuration.

THE PASS-THROUGH. `Api/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs`: `AddAnalysisRecordAuthorizationFilter` (:35-45) builds the filter in `AuthorizationMode.AnalysisAccess`. `InvokeAsync` (:89-112) checks only that an oid resolves, then switches on the mode; the switch DEFAULT is `_ =&gt; await next(context)` (:110), which is fail-open for any unhandled mode. `AuthorizeAnalysisAccessAsync` (:185-212) parses `analysisId`, logs "document lookup pending" under the comment "TRACKED: GitHub #233" (:203-209) and returns `next(context)`. It makes no lookup and no access decision. `AuthorizeDocumentAccessAsync` (:121-174) is the working mode: `ExtractDocumentIds` (:218-241) takes `AnalysisExecuteRequest.DocumentIds`, `CreateAnalysisRequest.DocumentId` and any bare `Guid` argument, answers 400 "No document identifier found in request" when it finds none (:128-135), then calls `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` and returns 403 on deny, 500 on an exception (never next). /create and /execute share this mode through `AddAnalysisExecuteAuthorizationFilter` (:19-29).

HANDLERS. GET `GetAnalysis` (:661-678), export `ExportAnalysis` (:601-655) and save `SaveWorkingDocument` (:568-595) call `IAnalysisOrchestrationService` with no check; their `KeyNotFoundException` branches (:587-590, :647-650, :674-677) return `{ error = "Analysis {analysisId} not found" }`, which echoes the id. `Services/Ai/AnalysisOrchestrationService.cs`: `SaveWorkingDocumentAsync` :90-114, `ExportAnalysisAsync` :117-, `GetAnalysisAsync` :282-312, all through `AnalysisDocumentLoader.GetOrReloadFromDataverseAsync` (:227-267), which serves a Redis copy keyed by tenant + analysis id on a hit and otherwise reads through the app-only `IAnalysisDataverseService` (`Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:383-408`, a ServiceClient as the BFF identity). Export places `sprk_workingdocument` into the DOCX/PDF bytes or an OBO email to caller-chosen recipients. Save goes to `Services/Ai/WorkingDocumentService.cs:91-218`, which reads `sprk_analysis.sprk_matterid` (:106-110) and that matter's `sprk_containerid` app-only, then `SpeFileStore.UploadSmallAsync` app-only; with no container it rewrites `sprk_analysis.sprk_workingdocument` with the same text. ⚠️ `sprk_matterid` is NOT in the MCP-verified sprk_analysis column list (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/sprkAnalysis.ts:200-225`), which lists `_sprk_documentid_value`, `_sprk_outputfileid_value`, `_sprk_playbook_value`, `_sprk_agreementtype_value`, `_sprk_regardingmatter_value`, `_sprk_regardingproject_value`, `_sprk_regardingdocument_value`, `_sprk_regardingbudget_value`, `_sprk_regardingcommunication_value`, `_sprk_regardinginvoice_value`, `_sprk_regardingrecordtype_value`, `sprk_regardingrecordid`. If the column is absent live, the SPE branch of save can never run (its retrieve faults and the catch falls back).

ANCHORS. An analysis is anchored by `sprk_documentid` and/or a typed regarding lookup. `DataverseServiceClientImpl.CreateAnalysisAsync` (:431-473) requires a document or a regarding target (FR-D9); `PopulateAnalysisRegardingAsync` / `StageAnalysisRegardingFields` (:484-) write the typed lookup from `RegardingRecordType.GetRegardingLookupFieldByEntity` (`Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:1254-1259`: sprk_matter → sprk_regardingmatter, sprk_project → sprk_regardingproject) plus the polymorphic resolver pair. Task 156 and owner round 8 item 3 treat analysis as an intermediate whose own `sprk_regarding{core}` columns carry a core-ancestor stamp; those columns are part of the live lookup sweep in step 0.

FORK. `ForkAnalysis` (:1136-1287): validates the body in this order (priorSessionId, name, DocumentId; :1147-1158, each a 400 built by `AnalysisProblem`), resolves the caller oid, loads the prior session and answers 404 when it is missing or not the caller's (:1170-1199, issue #863), then `CreateAnalysisAsync(request.DocumentId, request.Name, playbookId: request.PlaybookId)` app-only (:1207), mints a session bound to that document (:1230) and archives the prior one. `AiAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/AiAuthorizationFilter.cs:81-85`) calls `next` when `ExtractDocumentIds` (:130-153) finds no `DocumentAnalysisRequest`/`Guid` argument, which is always the case for `AnalysisForkRequest` (`Api/Ai/AnalysisForkContracts.cs:27`: PriorSessionId, DocumentId, Name, PlaybookId, HostContext). Nothing checks the caller's access to DocumentId or PlaybookId.

PROMOTE. `PromoteSession` (:1314-1454): validates sessionId and name (:1323-1331), checks tid only; `sessionManager.GetSessionAsync(tenantId, request.SessionId)` (:1344) with NO owner comparison (contrast fork :1186-1194); the one-time-bind guard returns a 400 for an already-bound session (:1351-1359) BEFORE any owner check, so today it also reveals that another user's session exists and is bound; regarding validated for shape only (:1366-1378, type trimmed and lower-cased, closed set sprk_matter | sprk_project); document = body DocumentId, else the session's own `DocumentId` (:1383-1393, which was caller-chosen at session create, sweep finding #24, task 164); `CreateAnalysisAsync` app-only with `playbookId: request.PlaybookId ?? session.PlaybookId` (:1405); `PromoteSessionToAnalysisAsync` rewrites the session's HostContext and the sprk_aichatsummary FK (:1422). `AnalysisPromoteRequest` (`Api/Ai/AnalysisPromoteContracts.cs:36`): SessionId, Name, DocumentId?, PlaybookId?, RegardingEntityType?, RegardingEntityId?, RegardingEntityName?. `ChatSession.OwnerOid` is nullable (`Models/Ai/Chat/ChatSession.cs:127`); fork treats a null owner as not-yours. `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SessionOwnershipGuardTests.cs:38-64` `BodyScopedSessionRoutes` has one row per FILE; the AnalysisEndpoints.cs row (:47-50) describes only /fork, so it silently exempts /promote too. Live callers: `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/useReviewedDocumentAnalysis.ts:37-42` (body {sessionId, name} only, relies on the session-document fallback; treats any non-OK as benign) and `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/HistoryOverlay.tsx:854-880` (adds regardingEntityType/Id/Name; shows the server's ProblemDetails `detail` text to the user on failure). Neither sends playbookId.

EXECUTE. `ExecuteAnalysis` (:256-): the filter already requires Read on every `DocumentIds` entry (`Services/Ai/AiAuthorizationService.cs:164-221`, Read only, None on any fault). The handler then returns 503 when Analysis is disabled (:276-281), 400 for multiple documents when not enabled (:284-289) and 400 for a missing PlaybookId (:294-303, a JSON `{ error }` body written to the response). Document-profile branch: `consumerRouting.ResolveAsync(ConsumerTypes.DocumentProfile)` (:333) equals `request.PlaybookId` → `ExecuteDocumentProfilePipelineAsync` (:858-) writes the document's profile fields through the app-only `IDocumentDataverseService.UpdateDocumentFieldsAsync` (:976) and enqueues RAG indexing (:995). Engine branch: `playbookOrchestrationService.ExecuteAsync` (:448) runs whatever `PlaybookId` the caller sends; there is no playbook-use check and no write-right check. `Services/Ai/PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs` loads nodes with `INodeService.GetNodesAsync(playbookId)` (:247); a playbook with ZERO nodes runs Legacy mode (:249-256), which delegates to `AnalysisOrchestrationService.ExecutePlaybookAsync` (:336-) and writes the document's profile outputs (`StoreDocumentProfileOutputsAsync`, :988) and enqueues RAG indexing (:1032). Node-based mode dispatches each node on `node.SprkExecutortype` directly (:1059-1075; a null value fails the node, there is no fallback) through `INodeExecutorRegistry.GetExecutor` (:1130). Side-effecting node executors (for example `Services/Ai/Nodes/UpdateRecordNodeExecutor.cs`, `CreateNotificationNodeExecutor.cs`, `SendEmailNodeExecutor.cs`, `CreateTaskNodeExecutor.cs`, `DeliverToIndexNodeExecutor.cs`) act as the app. `request.AnalysisId` is used only to build the caller's own notification link (:714). Live callers: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useAiSummary.ts:349` (Document Upload wizard; sends the "Document Profile" playbook, so it takes the profile branch), `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx:682`, and the SemanticSearchControl combined summary (`src/client/pcf/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl.tsx:870`, which hands the wizard its documents). All send documentIds plus playbookId. No src client calls GET, export, save or fork (grep of src/**/*.{ts,tsx} for "api/ai/analysis/", 2026-10-02).

REUSE — THE EXISTING MACHINERY (read each before writing code):
  • `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs`, task 130) is the ONE per-route evaluator. Its constructor is public: `new FinanceAuthorizationFilter(AuthorizationService, Func&lt;EndpointFilterInvocationContext, FinanceAuthorizationTargets&gt; resolveTargets, FinanceDenial denial, CallerRecordAccessProbe? probe)` (:263-273). `InvokeAsync` (:292-370) returns a `FinanceAuthorizationTargets.Rejection` before any rights query, denies when there are zero checks (`sdap.access.deny.no_target`), forwards the caller token or null (both paths deny on null), evaluates each `FinanceAuthorizationCheck` (:125-163) and denies on any exception (`sdap.access.error.system_failure`). Paths (`FinanceCheckPath`, :102-123): Document = `AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` against sprk_documents with an operation key; Record = `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(userId, entitySet, id, token)` + `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights`; Privilege = `CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync` (OBO, WhoAmI, RetrieveUserSetOfPrivilegesByNames, uncached, `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:386-`), built with `FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege(privilegeName, entitySet, source)`. Denial `FinanceDenial.UniformNotFound` renders `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound(httpContext)` (:280-290: constant title/detail, reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.record_unavailable`, correlationId, never the id); `FinanceDenial.Forbidden` renders `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden(reasonCode, traceId)`. Its reason-code and entity-set constants are at :222-256. This task builds check lists and hands them to this evaluator; it does not write a second evaluation loop.
  • `IAiAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync(user, documentIds, httpContext, ct)` (`Services/Ai/IAiAuthorizationService.cs:89-93`, impl `AiAuthorizationService.cs:48-221`): Read on sprk_documents over OBO through the same `IAccessDataSource.GetUserAccessAsync` the Document path uses. It stays the decision for the EXISTING DocumentAccess Read checks on /create and /execute; new checks go through the evaluator above.
  • `OperationAccessPolicy` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs`): "read" = Read (:163), "write" = Write (:242), "entity.associate_document" = AppendTo (:213; the key `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.AssociateContentOperation` already uses for "put content into a record's container"), "finance.attach_invoice" = AppendTo (:193, task 130's precedent for "AppendTo on each parent a new app-created row's lookups point at", kept separate so deny logs name the operation). `HasRequiredRights(rights, operation)` (:320). `DataverseAccessRightsMapper` maps AppendToAccess into the snapshot; `DataverseAccessDataSource` returns AccessRights.None for a missing record and on every fault (:351-364, :465-470).
  • `RecordContainerResolver.IsRecordNotFound(ex)` (`Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs:1939-1941`, internal static, typed on error code 0x80040217): the "row does not exist" test. Do not substring-match messages.
  • `IGenericEntityService.RetrieveAsync(entity, id, columns, ct)` (`Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs:12`): the app-only read of the analysis's ANCHOR ids (never content), the same seam `WorkingDocumentService.cs:106` uses.
  • `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:174-`, map :115-155, internal static): contact → contacts, sprk_matter → sprk_matters, sprk_project → sprk_projects, sprk_invoice → sprk_invoices, sprk_workassignment → sprk_workassignments, sprk_event → sprk_events, sprk_todo → sprk_todos. It has NO sprk_budget, sprk_communication or sprk_document entry.
  • `IPlaybookService.GetPlaybookAsync(id)` (`IsPublic`, `OwnerId` = the playbook's `_ownerid_value`, a systemuserid) and `PlaybookService.EntitySetName` = "sprk_analysisplaybooks" (`Services/Ai/PlaybookService.cs:34`, private const). Playbook team shares are real Dataverse POA shares (`PlaybookSharingService.GrantAccessToTeamAsync`, :316-); `IsPublic` is an app flag, not a Dataverse share (`SetOrganizationWideAsync` :342-360 only logs).
  • ⚠️ `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter` OwnerOrSharedOrPublic (`Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs:116-147`) is NOT reusable as-is: it compares `playbook.OwnerId` (a systemuserid) with `CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId` (an Entra oid) at :125, and `UserHasSharedAccessAsync` (`PlaybookSharingService.cs:215-272`) repeats that comparison and queries `teammemberships?$filter=systemuserid eq {oid}` (:284). Both GUID spaces differ, so owner and team grants never match and the decision reduces to `IsPublic` (sweep noteworthy, ai-b, `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs:125`). It also reads the id from the route value "id" (:106-114) and answers 404 for an unknown playbook (:117-122) but 403 for a denied one. Its existing behaviour on its own routes is task 164's.
  • `INodeService.GetNodesAsync(playbookId)` (`Services/Ai/INodeService.cs:17-19`) and `PlaybookNodeDto.SprkExecutortype` (`Models/Ai/PlaybookNodeDto.cs:60`, `ExecutorType` enum `Services/Ai/Nodes/INodeExecutor.cs:128-`): the same source and field PlaybookOrchestrationService dispatches on.
  • `CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId(user)` and the fork's owner comparison (`AnalysisEndpoints.cs:1170-1194`): the #863 session-owner pattern.
  • Caching: `GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` and the Document path go through `CachedAccessDataSource`, which caches None for up to 60 s (C12, task 132). The Privilege path is uncached.

GUARDS. `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs` (task 074): `GovernedFiles` (:126-) does not include Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs today. ⚠️ Rule A (`EveryGovernedRouteCarriesPerResourceAuthorizationOrANamedWaiver`, :882) credits any `.Add…AuthorizationFilter(` call by NAME through `FilterMarker` (:1898-), and Rule B (`NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative`, :1107) passes `AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs` because its text contains "AuthorizationService" (as part of IAiAuthorizationService; `DecisionServices` :1274-1296). So all six routes READ as gated to the structural guard today, while four of them decide nothing. The structural guard cannot prove this task; the real-host deny tests and the seeded proofs below are the proof. Task 167 (owner round 9 item 3) extends the guard to every route file and adds Pending waivers for the 82 findings. `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests.cs:28-31` says the AI filters "check AccessRights.Read directly and never consult this policy"; after this task AnalysisAuthorizationFilter does consult it, so that note must change. `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-003-operation-rights-decisions.md:92` lists AnalysisAuthorizationFilter as out of scope for task 003; this task supersedes that line for the six routes.

EXISTING TESTS THAT WILL MOVE. Unit: `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilterTests.cs` (it pins the enum values at :312-317 and the AnalysisAccess 400s at :235-270). Contract (real `MapAnalysisEndpoints` in-process hosts): `tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/AnalysisForkEndpointContractTests.cs` (fixture :224-, registers `Mock.Of&lt;IAiAuthorizationService&gt;()` at :269), `AnalysisPromoteEndpointContractTests.cs` (fixture :392-, :437), `AnalysisEndpointsExecuteDispatchContractTests.cs` (fixture :165-, auth mock :208). Regression: `tests/integration/regression/Analysis/PromoteDurableFkVisibilityTests.cs`. SPE suite (full `Program` host): `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/AnalysisEndpointsIntegrationTests.cs` (`AnalysisTestFixture` :491-, loose `Mock&lt;IPlaybookService&gt;` and `Mock&lt;INodeService&gt;` at :694-695, `MockAiAuthorizationService` :960-). A loose mock returns null: a null playbook or a null node array DENIES under this task, so those fixtures must return explicit playbooks, nodes and rights. `ExecuteAnalysis_WithPlaybookNotFound_ReturnsErrorChunk` (:284-330) asserts a 200 SSE error chunk for an unknown playbook; under this task an unknown playbook is a 403 before the stream, so that test's expectation is inverted on purpose. The task-130 recording fakes to reuse (internal nested types in the same integration test assembly): `FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.RecordingAccessDataSource` (:865-) and `RecordingPrivilegeProbe` (:797-), registered as at :950-955.</background>
