  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Re-verify every anchor in the background (line numbers drift). Check whether tasks 146, 164 and 167 are on this branch and record it. READ-ONLY live queries in dev, results recorded in the task note: (a) every Lookup attribute on sprk_analysis with its targets (`EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_analysis')/Attributes/Microsoft.Dynamics.CRM.LookupAttributeMetadata?$select=LogicalName,Targets`), and whether `sprk_matterid` exists; (b) the EntitySetName of every anchor target type; (c) row counts of active sprk_analysis rows with each anchor populated, with NO anchor populated, and with only the polymorphic pair; (d) the playbook ids each shipped execute consumer sends (useAiSummary, DocumentEmailWizard, SemanticSearch combined summary), with each playbook's IsPublic, its node count and its node executor types; (e) the exact name of the Create privilege on sprk_analysis (`privileges?$filter=startswith(name,'prvCreatesprk_')`), and, for the Spaarke security roles assigned to ordinary users, the depth at which they hold Create on sprk_analysis, AppendTo on sprk_document, sprk_matter and sprk_project, Write on sprk_document, and Read on sprk_analysisplaybook.</step>
    <step order="1">Implement the AnalysisAccess mode (anchor retrieve → classified anchors → Read on all, AND → evaluated by FinanceAuthorizationFilter with UniformNotFound), make the switch default deny, and make the three handlers' KeyNotFoundException branches return the uniform 404. Add the save destination AppendTo only if step 0 found `sprk_matterid`.</step>
    <step order="2">Fork and promote: the "analysis.attach" key, the Create-privilege constant, the shared body validators, the two new extension methods replacing `AddAiAuthorizationFilter()`, the promote handler's owner check (before the already-bound 400) and its session-document check. Update the SessionOwnershipGuardTests row so it names /fork and /promote and says what each handler checks.</step>
    <step order="3">Playbook-use decision (static method on PlaybookAuthorizationFilter) and the side-effect classification next to ExecutorType; then execute: `AddAnalysisRunAuthorizationFilter()` chained after the existing filter, the missing-PlaybookId 400, the profile-branch Write check, the engine-branch playbook-use check and the Write-on-every-document rule (empty node array, null executor type or side-effecting node). Apply the playbook-use decision to fork and promote body PlaybookIds.</step>
    <step order="4">Guards: RouteAuthorizationGuardTests per the guard constraint; the OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests scope note; delete the #233 placeholder and correct the remarks.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests (the closed set in the acceptance criteria), fixture updates (explicit allow/deny decisions, playbooks and nodes; the one inverted SPE expectation), and the seeded proofs (each seed applied from a backup, the affected suites run, the seed shown to turn a named test red, the source restored byte-identical). Record each seed and its red tests in the note.</step>
    <step order="6">Build; affected + full BFF unit + NetArchTest + both integration suites in full; publish size and CVE check; `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="7">Write notes/task-162-ai-analysis-route-authorization.md: step-0 live facts, the anchor classification, the side-effect classification, the 167/146/164 state, what 164 must reuse (the playbook-use method, the side-effect list, the unchecked session-derived PlaybookId), the seed table, and the manual live gate checklist for the main session. Set this task's TASK-INDEX.md status cell to `✅ [done]` only when the code criteria are met, with the live gate marked pending.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Step 0 finds active sprk_analysis rows whose only anchors have no entity set in EntityAccessFilter (for example sprk_regardingbudget or sprk_regardingcommunication), rows with no anchor at all, or rows whose only link is the polymorphic pair. This task would make them unreadable for everyone. STOP and report the counts. Do not add an entity-set map entry, and do not pick a rule for communications (they have their own ICommunicationAccessFilter seam).</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 0 shows the Spaarke roles assigned to ordinary users do NOT hold Create on sprk_analysis, or AppendTo on sprk_document, sprk_matter or sprk_project, at any depth, so G5 would deny every fork or promote (including HistoryOverlay "set related" and the reviewed-document promote). STOP and report the roles, privileges and depths. Do not drop the privilege or AppendTo check, and do not edit roles.</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 0 shows a shipped execute consumer sends a playbook that is neither public nor readable by ordinary users, or one that is side-effecting under constraint (5)-(6) (including a zero-node Legacy playbook), so a user with Read but not Write on the documents is denied by this task. STOP and report the playbook, its nodes and the consumer. Do not widen the rule and do not exempt the playbook by id.</trigger>
    <trigger>A node's executor type cannot be determined before the run from `GetNodesAsync` + `SprkExecutortype` (for example the orchestrator starts resolving it from somewhere else during execution). STOP and present options per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than guessing the type or treating every playbook as side-effecting without reporting it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Task 164 has landed a playbook-use or side-effect decision whose semantics differ from this task's constraints (for example it keeps the oid-versus-systemuserid owner comparison, or treats a missing executor type or a zero-node playbook as read-only). STOP and bring the difference to the main session. Do not ship two rules for the same question.</trigger>
    <trigger>You conclude the save route's SPE destination must be repointed (for example `sprk_matterid` does not exist and a regarding matter should receive the file). STOP: that is a functional change outside this authorization task. Record the finding and continue with the rest.</trigger>
    <trigger>A check cannot be placed in an endpoint filter without violating an ADR (for example ADR-008), the evaluator cannot be reused without editing FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs, or the fix needs an ADR exception. STOP and use the CLAUDE.md §6.5 format. Do not move the check into a service silently and do not fork the evaluator.</trigger>
    <trigger>The manual live gate shows a legitimate user denied on a shipped flow (the Document Upload wizard AI summary, the DocumentEmailWizard summary, the SemanticSearch combined summary, HistoryOverlay "set related", or the reviewed-document promote). STOP and report the flow, the user's rights on the target and the denying check. Do not widen to app-only or drop the check.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`AnalysisAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs`) ALREADY declares the AnalysisAccess mode for exactly these routes and leaves it as a placeholder (:185-212). The evaluator exists: `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (task 130) with its Document, Record and Privilege paths, `FinanceAuthorizationTargets`, `FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege` and `UniformRecordNotFound` (:102-425), over `AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` / `GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` + `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights` and `CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync`. So do the #863 owner comparison (`AnalysisEndpoints.cs:1170-1194`), `RecordContainerResolver.IsRecordNotFound` (:1939-1941), `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet`, `IPlaybookService.GetPlaybookAsync` and `PlaybookService.EntitySetName`. `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter`'s OwnerOrSharedOrPublic decision exists but compares an Entra oid with a systemuserid (:125; `PlaybookSharingService.cs:232`, :284), so it cannot be reused as-is. Grep for a side-effect classification of `ExecutorType` (SideEffect / IsWriteNode / HasSideEffects under Services/Ai, 2026-10-02) found only chat-tool gating (`Services/Ai/Chat/SideEffectGateAIFunction.cs` and related), not node executors. OperationAccessPolicy has AppendTo keys for documents into records ("entity.associate_document") and invoices onto parents ("finance.attach_invoice"), none for an analysis onto its parents.</existing>
    <extension>Yes. No new filter class, service, DI registration or entity-set map. Implement the existing AnalysisAccess mode; add three modes to the existing AnalysisAuthorizationFilter that only DECLARE checks and hand them to the existing FinanceAuthorizationFilter evaluator; add one policy key next to its two AppendTo siblings; add the playbook-use decision as one static method on the existing PlaybookAuthorizationFilter (not a second filter); add the side-effect list next to the enum it classifies. "entity.associate_document" and "finance.attach_invoice" are not reused for fork/promote because deny logs would name the wrong operation and neither carries the Read the fork's session needs (task 130 made the same choice).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any signed-in user reads any analysis's AI working document by id (including analyses of documents under secure matters), downloads it as DOCX or emails it to recipients they choose, and makes the BFF write it app-only into the matter's SPE container. Any user creates analyses app-only that attach to documents, matters or projects they cannot see (they appear on that record's Analyses tab) and rebinds a colleague's chat session. A read-only user overwrites a document's AI profile fields, re-triggers its indexing and runs any playbook, including side-effecting ones, against it. Without the analysis.attach key the G5 AppendTo check has no policy entry to evaluate, and OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests fails on an unknown operation.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

