  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/ai/analysis/{analysisId:guid} (finding #2): (a) a caller with Read on every populated anchor gets 200 with the same payload as today; (b) a caller lacking Read on ANY one populated anchor gets the uniform 404, and `IAnalysisOrchestrationService.GetAnalysisAsync` is not invoked (asserted on the substituted seam); (c) a non-existent analysis id, an analysis with no populated anchor, an analysis whose only link is the polymorphic pair, an anchor retrieve that faults, an anchor of a type with no entity set, and a request with no forwarded bearer token each get the uniform 404 with the service not invoked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/analysis/{analysisId:guid}/export (finding #1): the same six deny cases as GET answer the uniform 404, and `ExportAnalysisAsync` is not invoked (so no file bytes are returned and no email or Teams message is sent). A caller with Read on every anchor gets the existing 200 or file response.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/analysis/{analysisId:guid}/save (finding #50): the same six deny cases answer the uniform 404, and neither `SaveWorkingDocumentAsync` nor any SPE upload nor any Dataverse write is invoked. If step 0 found `sprk_analysis.sprk_matterid`: a caller with Read on every anchor but no AppendTo on that matter gets the uniform 404 with no upload, and the rights query names the matter and the sprk_matters set. If step 0 did not find it: the note records this, and `WorkingDocumentService.SaveToSpeAsync`'s destination code is unchanged in the diff. A caller with the required rights gets the existing 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Uniform answer on the three analysis-id routes: the responses for a non-existent id, a denied id, a no-anchor analysis, an anchor-read fault and a handler `KeyNotFoundException` after the check passed are byte-identical apart from correlation/trace ids. None contains the analysis id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Anchor rule: (a) an analysis whose document is readable and whose regarding matter is not is denied (AND, not OR); (b) a document anchor is checked on the document path (`IAccessDataSource.GetUserAccessAsync` with the document id), and matter, project, work assignment and invoice anchors on the record path with exactly sprk_matters / sprk_projects / sprk_workassignments / sprk_invoices as the entity-set argument (asserted on the recording IAccessDataSource); (c) an anchor type with no entity set in `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` denies; (d) a test names every Lookup attribute the step-0 live sweep returned for sprk_analysis as anchor or non-anchor, and fails on an unclassified one; (e) the anchor retrieve selects only columns in that snapshot.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/analysis/fork (finding #51): (a) a caller without the Create privilege on sprk_analysis gets 403 reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_privilege`; (b) a body DocumentId on which the caller lacks Read or lacks AppendTo gets 403 reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights`; (c) a non-existent DocumentId gets the identical 403; (d) a body PlaybookId that is not public and not readable by the caller, or that does not exist, gets the identical 403; (e) in (a)-(d) `CreateAnalysisAsync`, `CreateSessionAsync` and `ArchiveSessionAsync` are not invoked; (f) an empty DocumentId, priorSessionId or name gets the existing 400 with its existing text and no rights query made; (g) a caller with the privilege, Read and AppendTo gets 201 as today; (h) the prior-session ownership 404 is unchanged; (i) `AddAiAuthorizationFilter` no longer appears in the /fork chain.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/analysis/promote (finding #22): (a) a session owned by another user, or with a null OwnerOid, gets the 404 "Session not found" body, byte-identical to a missing session apart from correlationId, and neither `CreateAnalysisAsync` nor `PromoteSessionToAnalysisAsync` is invoked; (b) another user's session that is ALREADY bound gets that same 404, not the already-bound 400; (c) a caller without the Create privilege gets 403, nothing written; (d) a regarding sprk_matter or sprk_project on which the caller lacks Read or AppendTo gets 403, nothing written, and the rights query used sprk_matters or sprk_projects respectively; (e) a body DocumentId the caller cannot Read or AppendTo gets 403, nothing written; (f) with no body DocumentId, a session DocumentId the caller cannot Read or AppendTo gets 403 with the same body as (e), nothing written; (g) a non-existent regarding id, document id or playbook id gets the same 403 as a denied one; (h) a malformed regarding (wrong type, missing id) or an empty sessionId or name gets the existing 400 with no rights query made; (i) the caller's own session with the required rights gets 201 as today, both with only {sessionId, name} (the useReviewedDocumentAnalysis shape) and with a regarding matter (the HistoryOverlay shape); (j) `AddAiAuthorizationFilter` no longer appears in the /promote chain; (k) SessionOwnershipGuardTests' AnalysisEndpoints.cs row names both /fork and /promote and what each handler checks.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/ai/analysis/execute (finding #52): (a) a document the caller cannot Read still gets the existing 403 (existing behaviour and body); (b) a request with no PlaybookId gets the existing 400 body with no consumer-routing, playbook or node lookup made; (c) document-profile branch: a caller with Read but not Write on the document gets 403 before `UpdateDocumentFieldsAsync`, before the indexing enqueue and before any AI call (asserted on the seams); a caller with Write runs the profile as today; an `IConsumerRoutingService` fault denies; (d) engine branch: a playbook that is not public and on which the caller has no Dataverse Read gets 403 and `IPlaybookOrchestrationService.ExecuteAsync` is not invoked; a non-existent PlaybookId gets the identical 403; a public playbook needs no Read on the playbook row; (e) engine branch: with a side-effecting node, with a node whose `SprkExecutortype` is null, or with zero nodes, a caller with Read but not Write on any one document gets 403 and ExecuteAsync is not invoked; with only read-only nodes and Read on every document the stream runs as today; a `GetNodesAsync` fault or null result denies; (f) the side-effect classification test enumerates every `ExecutorType` value and fails on an unclassified one; (g) POST /api/ai/analysis/create behaves exactly as before (Read on the document; its chain unchanged in the diff; its existing tests unchanged and green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AnalysisAuthorizationFilter: an `AuthorizationMode` value with no case (for example `(AuthorizationMode)99`) denies with 403 and never calls next (unit test); the existing enum values keep their numbers (the :312-317 pin stays green); the "TRACKED: GitHub #233" placeholder and the "placeholder" remarks are gone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Playbook-use decision: one static method on PlaybookAuthorizationFilter is the only implementation (execute, fork and promote call it); it never compares an Entra oid with a playbook OwnerId; `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.InvokeAsync` and its two extension methods are unchanged in the diff, and `PlaybookAuthorizationFilterTests` passes unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reach and completeness: a test through the REAL `MapAnalysisEndpoints` host enumerates every endpoint the group maps (from the host's EndpointDataSource; seven today, including /create) and fails if any route under /api/ai/analysis has no entry in the test's deny-case table. For each of the seven routes, a caller the seams report as None is denied through the real host.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests: either (167 on branch) the Pending waivers for these six routes are deleted, or (167 absent) `Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs` is in GovernedFiles with Scope.RouteLevelGate and a reason. In both cases no waiver names a route in AnalysisEndpoints.cs, Rule A, Rule B, RuleBCoversEveryFilterRuleACredits, the census and NoWaiverIsStale pass, `FilterMarker` and `DecisionServices` are unchanged, and the note records which case applied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new logical-name → entity-set map exists and no "sprk_analysisplaybooks" literal is added; `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType`, `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` and FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs are unchanged in the diff; no new filter class or service is added; OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests passes with "analysis.attach" present and its :28-31 scope note describes the AI filters correctly; the Create-privilege constant is pinned by a test to the name step 0 read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeded proofs, each shown to turn at least one named test red and then restored byte-identical: S1 AnalysisAccess returns next (pass-through restored); S2 AND changed to OR across anchors; S3 the regarding-matter column dropped from the anchor select; S4 the no-anchor deny removed (zero checks turned into next); S5 a handler KeyNotFoundException body echoing the id; S6 the fork DocumentId check removed; S7 the fork/promote Create-privilege check removed; S8 "analysis.attach" weakened to Read only; S9 the promote owner comparison removed; S10 the promote owner comparison moved after the already-bound 400; S11 the promote session-document check removed; S12 the execute profile-branch Write check removed; S13 the playbook-use check removed; S14 the playbook-use decision switched to the oid-versus-OwnerId comparison; S15 one side-effecting ExecutorType removed from the classification; S16 the zero-node (Legacy) case treated as read-only; S17 the switch default restored to next. The seed table is in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover exactly the behaviours above plus the fail-closed branches named in the constraints; existing fixtures (fork, promote, execute-dispatch contract tests, PromoteDurableFkVisibilityTests if affected, the Spe.Integration.Tests AnalysisTestFixture) return explicit allow or deny decisions, playbooks and nodes; `ExecuteAnalysis_WithPlaybookNotFound_ReturnsErrorChunk` is the only existing test whose expectation changes (to 403 before the stream), and the note says why. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build green; the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite, NetArchTest and BOTH integration suites (tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests) run in full and green; publish size reported against a fresh origin/master build per CLAUDE.md §10 (both absolute sizes, delta, zip tool, equal file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, main session, existing non-admin test users in their current business units; verification reads only). (a) For an analysis anchored to a document user U1 cannot read: GET, export (docx) and save as U1 each return 404, the analysis's modifiedon is unchanged and no new file appears in any container. (b) A user with Read on that document (and on every other anchor) gets 200 on GET and export. (c) A random GUID returns the identical 404. (d) U1 promoting its own session with regardingEntityId = a matter U1 cannot read gets 403, and no sprk_analysis with that name exists afterwards. (e) U1 forking its own session with that document gets 403, no analysis created. (f) U1 promoting another user's session id gets 404, and that session's sprk_aichatsummary.sprk_analysis is unchanged. (g) Execute with the document-profile playbook on a document U1 can Read but not Write gets 403 and the document's modifiedon is unchanged. (h) Users with the expected rights still complete the Document Upload wizard AI summary, the DocumentEmailWizard summary, the SemanticSearch combined summary, HistoryOverlay "set related" and the reviewed-document promote. Results go in notes/task-162-ai-analysis-route-authorization.md (ids redacted to the first 8 characters).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Sweep findings closed: #1 export (critical), #2 GET (critical), #22 promote (high), #50 save (medium), #51 fork (medium), #52 execute (medium); verifier traces in the scratchpad file idor-group-162.json and in workflow run wf_c2daa097-2f4. Decisions taken at authoring (the owner may revisit; each is recorded so it is not mistaken for an oversight): (1) an analysis is a child record and inherits from its parents: visible to anyone with Read on ALL of its anchors, with no creator or owner rule. The analysis row's OWN Dataverse rights are deliberately not consulted: today those rows are created app-only and owned by the BFF identity (task 146 changes the owner), so requiring them would deny honest callers. Round 9 says "the exact record"; once 146 has re-owned analysis rows, the owner may want Read on the analysis row itself added to the AND. (2) Fork and promote follow G5 (owner rounds 3b, 7 item 3, 9): Create privilege on sprk_analysis plus Read and AppendTo on every parent the new row points at. POST /api/ai/analysis/create, which creates the same row with only Read on the document, is NOT a sweep finding and stays unchanged here; the main session should ask the owner whether /create adopts G5 too, since it is now the weaker sibling. (3) Export requires Read, not the SPE download Write policy, because GET already returns the same text. (4) The playbook-use decision is Dataverse's own answer on the sprk_analysisplaybook row, or IsPublic; the existing OwnerOrSharedOrPublic code is not reused because it compares an oid with a systemuserid. (5) Execute's engine branch requires Write on the request's documents as the proxy for a side-effecting playbook; it does not check the rights a node needs on other records it writes (for example a CreateTask node's to-do). Related items NOT in this task (sweep "noteworthy", for the main session): GET /api/ai/chat/sessions/by-analysis/{analysisId} always 403s because AiAuthorizationFilter checks the analysis id as a document id; once this task lands, that route can use AddAnalysisRecordAuthorizationFilter (task 164's ChatEndpoints surface). GET /api/ai/chat/context-mappings/analysis/{analysisId} is safe only because its app-only retrieve names attributes that do not exist; the same filter is its gate if that is ever fixed. ReviewMemoEndpoints trust session.HostContext.EntityId as an sprk_analysis. Promote's session-derived PlaybookId and DocumentId were chosen at session create (sweep #24, task 164). PlaybookAuthorizationFilter's own routes keep the oid-versus-systemuserid defect until 164 switches them to the new method. The evaluator's log lines say "Finance authorization" because the class is task 130's; renaming it is out of scope. Caching: the Document and Record paths go through CachedAccessDataSource, which caches None for up to 60 s (C12, task 132); a newly granted reader may see the 404 or 403 for up to a minute. An analysis present only in the Redis cache and never persisted (if any still exist) now answers 404. This task supersedes task-003-operation-rights-decisions.md:92 ("AnalysisAuthorizationFilter out of scope") for these routes.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute; Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check are mandatory (FULL).</protocol>
    <executed date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-162" base="91a1c1c83" rigor="FULL" model="opus">
      <summary>GET /api/ai/analysis/{analysisId:guid}: Read on EVERY populated anchor as the caller, uniform 404 (GitHub #233 item 1 closed). POST /promote: G5 in the filter (prvCreatesprk_analysis + "analysis.attach" = Read|AppendTo on the body document and regarding matter/project + playbook-use decision); in the handler the session owner check runs right after GetSessionAsync, before the already-bound 400, and the session-derived document is checked as the caller. POST /execute: the unchanged Read filter, then a run filter (Write on every document for the document-profile branch or a playbook with zero nodes / a null executor type / a side-effecting node; playbook-use decision otherwise). The AuthorizationMode switch default denies. POST /fork, /{id}/save and /{id}/export were DELETED (owner round 10 item 1) with every service, option, package (QuestPDF) and test only they used. Every new check is evaluated by FinanceAuthorizationFilter (unchanged).</summary>
      <amendments-applied>Owner rounds 9-12 read. FinanceAuthorizationFilter not renamed or edited. Task 167 NOT on the branch: AnalysisEndpoints.cs added to GovernedFiles (RouteLevelGate), no waivers; ledger-input table in the note section 8. Round 10 item 1 applied: three routes deleted with evidence (note section 2). No impersonation code added.</amendments-applied>
      <escalations>
        <fired trigger="1" state="OPEN">221 of 994 active sprk_analysis rows have NO anchor (0 pair-only, 0 unresolvable-only; 4 carry a contact assignee). Implemented fail-closed per constraint (5): GET answers the uniform 404 for them. Only consumer affected: the Copilot agent's published getAnalysis (no first-party UI caller). The GET rule must NOT be integrated until the owner chooses: (a) accept (recommended), (b) fall back to the caller's own Read on the analysis row, (c) backfill. Note section 3. Also: something still creates anchorless analyses (latest 2026-10-02, 65 by the BFF app identity) - issue for the owner.</fired>
        <not-fired>2 (Core/Basic User hold Create sprk_analysis and AppendTo document/matter/project at Deep); 3 (Document Profile takes the profile branch; Summarize File is private but readable by the child-BU test user and read-only); 4 (dispatch reads SprkExecutortype from GetNodesAsync, the same source); 5 (164 not landed); 6 (save deleted; sprk_matterid does not exist live); 7 (ADR013_AiBoundaryTests FR-C6 resolved by section 6.5 Path C: the playbook lookup goes through the grandfathered PlaybookAuthorizationFilter IServiceProvider overload); 8 pending (manual live gate).</not-fired>
      </escalations>
      <justification-new-surface>
        <item name="AuthorizationMode.AnalysisPromote / AnalysisRun + AddAnalysisPromoteAuthorizationFilter / AddAnalysisRunAuthorizationFilter">Existing: AnalysisAuthorizationFilter already declares the modes for these routes (AnalysisAccess was the placeholder). Extension: yes - two modes on the existing filter, each only DECLARING FinanceAuthorizationChecks for the existing evaluator; no new filter class (AnalysisFork was not added: the fork route is deleted). Cost of doing nothing: any signed-in user rebinds a colleague's session and creates analyses app-only against records they cannot see (finding #22); a Read-only user overwrites a document's profile fields and runs any playbook (finding #52).</item>
        <item name="AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.LookupColumns / AnchorColumns / CreateAnalysisPrivilege / AnalysisAttachOperation">Existing: grep for an sprk_analysis anchor table found none; FinanceAuthorizationFilter.CreateInvoicePrivilege is the precedent for a pinned privilege constant. Extension: constants in the existing filter, not a new map (entity sets come from EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet). Cost: without the table the GET check has no columns to read; a misspelt privilege denies every promote.</item>
        <item name="OperationAccessPolicy key analysis.attach">Existing: entity.associate_document and finance.attach_invoice are AppendTo keys for other acts (grep OperationAccessPolicy.cs). Extension: not reused - deny logs would name the wrong operation and neither carries Read. Cost: the G5 AppendTo check has no policy entry and OperationAccessRule denies it as unknown_operation.</item>
        <item name="PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.BuildPlaybookUseCheckAsync (two overloads)">Existing: InvokeAsync's OwnerOrSharedOrPublic branch compares an oid with a systemuserid (PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs:125) and cannot be reused. Extension: one static method on the existing filter (not a second filter); the IServiceProvider overload keeps IPlaybookService out of the analysis filter (ADR-013 FR-C6). Cost: execute and promote run any playbook id the caller names.</item>
        <item name="ExecutorSideEffects (next to ExecutorType)">Existing: grep SideEffect|IsWriteNode|HasSideEffects under Services/Ai found only chat-tool gating (SideEffectGateAIFunction). Extension: a closed table next to the enum it classifies. Cost: execute cannot tell a read-only playbook from one that writes as the app, so it either over-denies every run or lets a Read-only caller trigger writes.</item>
        <item name="removed">No new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job, column or package. Removed: 3 routes, 4 export/PDF services, ExportServiceRegistry, 3 IExportService registrations, 4 AnalysisOptions flags, the ai.export.* metrics, the QuestPDF package, WorkingDocumentService.SaveToSpeAsync.</item>
      </justification-new-surface>
      <placement>In the BFF: existing BFF routes and filters; no new component (.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md section A). Package removed, none added; CVE check clean. Publish size (measured by the round-1 verifier per CLAUDE.md section 10, recorded in round 1): base 91a1c1c83 45.66 MB / 212 files, branch 35.11 MB / 190 files, delta -10.55 MB, PowerShell Compress-Archive Optimal, PDBs included, short-path fresh worktrees; the 22-file difference is exactly the deleted QuestPDF package's files. Under the 60 MB ceiling.</placement>
